# src/tychoc.c:7167 -- reserve mutates its array, and an array parameter is
# borrowed read-only. The message is SHORTER than push's at src/tychoc.c:7115:
# it carries no copy suggestion, which is why it is a rule of its own.
# tychoc1 ACCEPTED this under --typecheck until the check was ported into
# compiler/types/tcheck.ty; both now word it identically.
# expect: cannot mutate parameter 'xs' (it is borrowed read-only)
fn g(xs: [int]):
    reserve(xs, 8)

fn main():
    ys := [1, 2]
    g(ys)
